# The bytes of these files ARE the onchain commitment: `feedbackHash =
# keccak256(utf8(document))`. Git must therefore never transform them.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line normalisation, `-diff` keeps a tool from treating
# them as text to reformat. The canonical JCS form has no line break anyway — but
# relying on that property rather than on an explicit rule would be accepting
# that a Windows checkout could invalidate a verdict.
#
# The pattern targets the documents (`0x` + 64 hex, no extension) and leaves
# `index.json` as ordinary text: that one is not hashed.
0x* -text -diff
batch/0x* -text -diff
